                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone fixed-size='280' h='5389' id='132' is-fixed='true' name='Sheet 18 (2)' w='48750' x='750' y='86946'>
                  <layout-cache minwidth='422' type-h='fixed' type-w='scalable' />
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone fixed-size='280' h='5389' id='133' is-fixed='true' name='Sheet 26' w='49167' x='50000' y='86946'>
                  <layout-cache minwidth='382' type-h='fixed' type-w='scalable' />
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone fixed-size='280' h='5389' id='134' is-fixed='true' name='Sheet 26 (2)' w='49167' x='50000' y='86946'>
                  <layout-cache minwidth='402' type-h='fixed' type-w='scalable' />
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone h='1916' id='135' type-v2='text' w='98333' x='750' y='92455'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Neighborhood wealth is overwhelmingly predicted by </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>structural factors</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>, with a profound correlation between income and both </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>educational attainment</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> and </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>employment status</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>. High-income neighborhoods exhibit a massive concentration of advanced degrees and labor force participation. Furthermore, the analysis reveals a crucial insight: the </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>gender pay gap widens substantially</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> as neighborhood income levels increase. Disability status, however, shows no significant variation across income groups.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='1916' id='136' type-v2='text' w='98333' x='750' y='92455'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Wile the </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Bronx</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> is established as the primary locus of economic hardship, it also has low labor force participation and lower educational atteinment levels. </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Manhattan</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> anchors the other extreme, while </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>Brooklyn, Queens, and Staten Island</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'> fill the complex middle ground. Where the increasing </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>gender pay gap in the wealthier Boroughs, </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='11'>acts as a universal pressure across all five boroughs. Disability rates remain approximately equal.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='2635' id='146' type-v2='text' w='98333' x='750' y='94731'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='20'>Final Conclusion</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The analysis confirms that economic disparity in New York City is </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>structurally embedded and highly contrasting</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>. The city is defined by a </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>geographic polarization</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>, with </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The Bronx</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'> isolated as the most vulnerable borough due to the lowest income and highest rent burden. This financial contrast is fundamentally driven by </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>structural factors</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>: extreme </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>racial concentration</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'> predicts economic outcome, resulting in a severe income gap and disproportionate poverty. Furthermore, the divide is amplified by </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>educational attainment</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'> and </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>employment status</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>, while the </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Gender Pay Gap widens significantly</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'> in affluent areas, revealing that the city&apos;s economic landscape is governed by powerful, reinforcing systemic patterns. </run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='2395' id='138' type-v2='text' w='98333' x='750' y='97617'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='11'>Data Sources:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>ACS 2018–2022 5-Year Estimates (U.S. Census Bureau):</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000'> Provides detailed demographic, social, economic, and housing data at various geographic levels (e.g., Census Tracts) - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#0000ff' fontname='Benton Sans Book' underline='true'>American Community Survey 5-Year Data (2009-2023)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>2020 Neighborhood Tabulation Areas (NTAs) shapefile — NYC Open Data:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000'> Provides the official boundaries for NYC NTAs, which are used for neighborhood-level spatial analysis - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#0000ff' fontname='Benton Sans Book' underline='true'>2020 Neighborhood Tabulation Areas (NTAs) | NYC Open Data</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>NYC Department of City Planning — ACS (with NTA geographies):</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000'> Provides a crossfile used to map ACS 5-year summary files directly to Neighborhood Tabulation Areas - </run>
                    <run auto-url='true' fontcolor='#000000' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://www.nyc.gov/content/planning/pages/resources/datasets/american-community-survey&amp;quot;'>https://www.nyc.gov/content/planning/pages/resources/datasets/american-community-survey</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000'> .</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
      <simple-id uuid='{A8812CB5-6367-4CFF-A17F-2AC2BF3EDC63}' />
